{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.fr_weight_homogeneous","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.fr_weight_homogeneous","kind":"theorem","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L202-L213","doc":"The FR-pulled-back weight is invariant under simultaneous\nrescaling of dim_q_sq and z_normalization by the same factor\n(homogeneity of the ratio).\n\nProvable directly via field arithmetic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.fr_weight_chi_scale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.fr_weight_chi_scale","kind":"theorem","line":193,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L193-L200","doc":"The FR-pulled-back weight scales linearly in χ^λ(e_K). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_ideal_4_1_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_ideal_4_1_value","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L184-L189","doc":"The chirality ideal at k = 3 has central projector value 1\n(placeholder; the full Hecke-algebra projector requires the\nq-Hecke representation infrastructure). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_ideal_4_1_label","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_ideal_4_1_label","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L179-L182","doc":"The chirality ideal at k = 3 is labelled \"4_1\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.depthStratifiedFR_chiralityIdeal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.depthStratifiedFR_chiralityIdeal","kind":"def","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L148-L175","doc":"**Chirality-ideal model with the predicate read as its own\nwitness.**  `knot_ideal_at_k` is real at `k = 3`\n(`chirality_ideal_4_1`) and a `\"?\"`-labelled zero projector\nelsewhere.  The conjectural field is not: `fr_pullback_at_low_k` is\n*defined* to be `fun q _k => q = 1`, so\n`fr_pullback_classical : ∀ k, fr_pullback_at_low_k 1 k` unfolds to\n`1 = 1` and closes by `rfl`, uniformly in `k`.  No Frobenius\nreciprocity, induced representation or depth stratum is encoded;\nthe field is satisfied by choosing the predicate to be the equation\nthe field asserts.\n\nThe classical-limit case genuinely is provable in principle, via\nMathlib's `Representation.induced` plus the pending Specht-module\nAPI — that is what a real model would have to supply here.\n\n**A `def`, not an `instance`, since 2026-08-24**, and given a name:\nit was anonymous, so resolution supplied it for every field under\nthe generated name `instDepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity`.\n\nCallers name it: `letI := depthStratifiedFR_chiralityIdeal R`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.fr_pullback_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.fr_pullback_classical","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L146-L146","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.fr_pullback_at_low_k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.fr_pullback_at_low_k","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L145-L145","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.knot_ideal_at_k","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.knot_ideal_at_k","kind":"def","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L144-L144","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L143-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity","kind":"class","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L130-L146","doc":"The DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity conjecture as a class.\n\nFields:\n- `knot_ideal_at_k`: the distinguished knot ideal at each\n  k ≤ 3 (only k = 3 has a named instance currently).\n- `fr_pullback_at_low_k`: predicate identifying the\n  (q, k) pairs where the FR pullback holds.\n- `fr_pullback_classical`: the classical-limit case\n  (provable in principle via Mathlib's Representation.induced;\n  pending Specht-module API).\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-cond, downstream theorems consume the\nclass via [Instance]. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:depth-stratified-frobenius-reciprocity","label":"conj:depth-stratified-frobenius-reciprocity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/depth-stratified-frobenius-reciprocity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.fr_weight_normalised","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.fr_weight_normalised","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L116-L128","doc":"The FR weight normalisation: if Z_norm = Σ dim_q²(μ) χ^μ(e_K)\nfor μ in a depth stratum, then summing the FR weights over\nthat stratum gives 1 (after the dim_q² · χ^μ(e_K) / n_q_fact\nnormalisation). Stated as a structural property of the\nZ_normalization choice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.fr_weight_transparent_reduces_to_uniform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.fr_weight_transparent_reduces_to_uniform","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L104-L114","doc":"Special case: when the projector character χ^λ(e_K) = 1\nuniformly across the depth stratum (the \"transparent\"\nprojector limit), and Z_normalization = 1 (single-block\nstratum), the FR weight equals the uniform weight.\n**Verified** unconditionally. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.frPulledBackWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.frPulledBackWeight","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L90-L102","doc":"The FR-pulled-back Wedderburn weight at depth k:\ndim_q²(λ) · χ^λ(e_{K_k*}) / ([n]_q! · Z_normalization)\n\nwhere Z_normalization is the partition-depth sum of\ndim_q²(μ) · χ^μ(e_{K_k*}).\n\nVerifiable identity: when χ^λ(e_K) = 1 (trivial projector,\ni.e. K is \"transparent\"), the FR weight reduces to the\nuniform weight times the depth-sum reciprocal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.uniformWedderburnWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.uniformWedderburnWeight","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L82-L88","doc":"The classical (uniform) Wedderburn weight at depth k:\ndim_q²(λ) / [n]_q!.  Defined unconditionally as a closed-form\nplaceholder; downstream code parametrises by the actual\npartition data. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_ideal_4_1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.chirality_ideal_4_1","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L71-L80","doc":"The distinguished chirality-channel ideal at k = 3:\n4_1 (figure-eight knot), as ranked best by the FR-pullback variance\ntest **under the textbook weight** `w_λ = dim_q²/[n]_q!` (PR #826).\nThe ranking is weight-family-dependent — see the module docstring —\nso this label records one family's answer, not a settled\nidentification. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DistinguishedKnotIdeal.knot_label","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DistinguishedKnotIdeal.knot_label","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L69-L69","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DistinguishedKnotIdeal.central_projector_value","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DistinguishedKnotIdeal.central_projector_value","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L68-L68","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DistinguishedKnotIdeal.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DistinguishedKnotIdeal.mk","kind":"ctor","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L67-L67","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.DistinguishedKnotIdeal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.DistinguishedKnotIdeal","kind":"structure","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocity.lean#L50-L69","doc":"The depth-k distinguished knot ideal as a central projector.\n\nFields:\n- `central_projector_value`: amplitude of the central projector\n  e_K at a partition (proxy for the full Hecke-algebra projector\n  in the abstract setting), valued in the generic base ring `R`.\n- `knot_label`: the name of the distinguished knot (\"4_1\"\n  at k = 3 *under the textbook weight* `dim_q²/[n]_q!` — the label is\n  family-relative, see the module docstring; pending for k = 1, k = 2).\n\n§7c: the FR-pullback weight algebra below is pure field arithmetic\n(a `dim_q²·χ / ([n]_q!·Z)` ratio), so it is stated over a generic\n`{R : Type*} [Field R]`. This module is now wholly on the algebraic\nside of the substrate→archimedean wall: the empirical decimal\n*variance records* (ordered `ℝ` literals) that used to sit further\ndown have been split out into the sibling\n`QOU.BraidKnot.DepthStratifiedFrobeniusReciprocityVariance`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}